    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "PREMISE",
      "narration_text": "The premise is genuinely good. Real health data is confidential, expensive, and often too small. Synthetic data promises a way around all three — privacy, scarcity, and bias — by learning a distribution instead of copying records.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "THE PREMISE",
            "headline": "Learn the distribution. Never copy the record.",
            "kicker": "privacy · scarcity · bias — three real problems"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-09T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14.1,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.0,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-09T19:15:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "GAN",
      "narration_text": "CTGAN does this with two networks. A generator invents rows. A discriminator tries to spot the fakes. They train against each other until neither can win, and whatever the generator produces at that point becomes your dataset.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "SynthGanDuel",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-09T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14.1,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.57,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:SynthGanDuel",
        "at": "2026-09-09T19:15:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "SETUP",
      "narration_text": "The notebook builds ten thousand patient records, trains CTGAN on them, and asks three questions. Is the synthetic data statistically faithful. Is it useful for modelling. And is it private.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "THE EXPERIMENT",
            "headline": "Fidelity. Utility. Privacy.",
            "kicker": "three claims — and the notebook answers yes to all three"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-09T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.59,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-09T19:15:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "TWIST",
      "narration_text": "But look at where the real data comes from. Age is a random integer. B M I is a random normal. Blood pressure, cholesterol, glucose, sleep, diabetes — every column drawn on its own, with no relationship to any other column.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "SynthRandomReveal",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-09T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15.6,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.53,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:SynthRandomReveal",
        "at": "2026-09-09T19:15:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "NUANCE",
      "narration_text": "That matters more than it sounds. Four derived columns do carry real structure, because they are computed from the others. Everything else is independent noise wearing medical labels.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "WHAT IS ACTUALLY IN THERE",
            "headline": "Independent noise, with medical column names.",
            "kicker": "the only real structure is the structure that was calculated"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-09T00:00:00"
          }
        }
