      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B19",
      "act": "PRIVACY",
      "narration_text": "The privacy claim rests on one number: the single smallest distance between any real and any synthetic record, out of one hundred million pairs. One extreme value, compared against a threshold with no stated origin, and no baseline for what real-to-real distance even looks like.",
